# "{T}, Sacrifice Lotus Petal: Add one mana of any color." A mana ability's costs are paid as any ability's are (CR 605.3a,
# 602.2b, 601.2h), together: the {T} is paid on the Petal while it is a permanent, so it is sacrificed tapped and its
# last-known information says so (CR 608.2h, 701.26a). `LeftBattlefield` reads the history in order: a tap recorded after
# the Petal had gone to the graveyard would not count as the Petal leaving tapped. The {B} it adds is checked in the pool.

[Bot1 Deck]
Lotus Petal
Island x19

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Lotus Petal.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Lotus Petal.Activate(Color: Black)
? Bot1.Mana = {B}
? LeftBattlefield = Lotus Petal (tapped)
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
LeftBattlefield = Lotus Petal (tapped)
Bot1.Graveyard = Lotus Petal
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 0
